8 1 Food and Nutrition Programs. RSA 189:11-a, VIII is repealed and reenacted to read as
9 follows:
10 VIII. All school districts with meal programs approved to operate through the United States
11 DepartmentofAgricultureshalladoptaschoolmealspolicythat:
12 (a) Prohibitsschoolsfromdenyingamealto,orservinganalternativemealto,astudent
13 withanunpaidstudentmealbalanceorwithoutfundstopayforameal.
14 (b) Prohibits schools from disposingof or taking away anyfood from a child that already
15 has been served to the child on account of the child having an unpaid student meal balance or
16 lackingthefundstopayforameal.
17 (c) Prohibits schools from identifying or stigmatizing a student as receiving a free,
18 reduced price or full-price meal or meals for which the child lacks funds to pay, including, but not
19 limited to, the use of tokens, stickers, stamps, or by placing the child's name on a published list of
20 personswithstudentmealdebt.
21 (d) Prohibits schools from limiting a student's participation in any school activities,
22 graduation ceremonies, field trips, athletics, activity clubs, or other extracurricular activities, or
23 access to materials, technology, or other items provided to students due to an unpaid student meal
24 balance.
25 (e) Prohibits schools from requiring a student to provide services or perform work,
26 includingcleaningdutiesorchores,topayforschoolmealsdebt.
27 (f) Requires schools to develop an outreach plan to encourage parent(s) or guardians(s)
28 toapplyforthefreeandreduced-pricemealsprogram.
29 (g) Authorizes schools to complete the application for free meals for the student
30 pursuanttoTitle7,Section245.6(d)oftheCodeofFederalRegulations.
31 (h) Requiresschooldistrictstoacceptvoluntarydonationstoalleviateschoolmealdebt.
32 2 EffectiveDate. ThisactshalltakeeffectJuly1,2025.
